{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "name": "Calibration grid",
  "_about": "For finding where things sit on the real screen: green lines every 100 px, faint ones every 50, labels are x/y in target pixels. Then two swatch strips, the same picture as a shader (top) and as pixels (bottom): grey steps 0..1 and four dark test colours, to compare the colour curve of the two paths. Then L1..L16, each on its OWN image layer: how many of them show counts the layers the car draws (with grid, labels and the two strips, L1..L4 showing means 8). Photograph it and the layouts get fitted to the photo.",
